nIU accessibility training\nNVDA basics\nAccess NVDA on an STC public desktop with IUanyWare\nVoiceOver basics\nVoiceOver for iOS basics\nVended software\nMinimum expectations for accessible vended software or web applications\nAccessibility questions to ask current or potential vendors\nQuick review of a VPAT\nMedium-level review of a VPAT, stage 1\nMedium-level review of a VPAT, stage 2\nPerform a full review of a VPAT\nScore VPATs to compare two or more products\nDetermine affected audiences for creating an Equally Effective Alternate Access Plan (EEAAP)\nIT compliance risks elevated with use of accessibility overlays\nGeneral accessibility information\nDisability inclusion\nTalking about disability\nModels of disability\nRange of abilities\nDisability etiquette\nBarriers to access\nDaily life with a disability\nTypes of impairments	KB0024650	KB0024650 v23.0	 when choosing between Google at IU My Drive and Microsoft <strong>OneDrive</strong> at IU PDF resources PDF	2.2006		2026-01-31 16:55:06.735766	2026-01-31 16:55:06.735766	0	994e1568476afadc2fc6a55b416d4308
10837	https://servicenow.iu.edu/kb?id=kb_article_view&sys_kb_id=9ccedd7e47743ad42fc6a55b416d43fc	Transcription services approved for use with institutional data at IU	Table of contents\nOverview\nData classifications and management standards for institutional data at IU\nWhere to store transcription files\nApproved transcription services for all data domains\nCarbonCopy\nMicrosoft 365 Copilot app\nApproved transcription services for research and health data\nAbsolute Marketing Research, LLC,\nAutomatic Sync Technologies\nAutomatic Transcription Services (ATS)\nGLOBO\nInfraware\nLandmark Associates, Inc.\nLumivero\nMicrosoft 365 transcription\nSonix.ai\nAccessibility service that may also provide transcription\nTranscription services not approved for use with institutional data\nOverview\nTranscription services are widely used across Indiana University. This article contains a list of transcription services that have been approved for use with\ninstitutional data\n, including data classified as\nRestricted or Critical\n, with a focus on services that are appropriate for work with research and health data. Transcription services that also offer translation are listed below.\nData classifications and management standards for institutional data at IU\nIf you are unsure whether you are storing individual or institutional files, see\nDetermine whether your files are individual (personal) or institutional\n.\nOfficial classifications for institutional data at IU are defined in\nManagement of Institutional Data (DM-01)\n. If you have questions about the classifications of institutional data at IU, consult the\nData Sharing and Handling (DSH) tool\nor contact the appropriate\nData Steward\n. For questions about research data, you can also consult IU Data Management's\nguidance on determining the classification for research data\n.\nWhere to store transcription files\nFor guidance about where to store transcription files after downloading them from the vendor, consult the following resources:\nSecureMyResearch Cookbook\n(for more, see\nAbout SecureMyResearch\nor email\nsecuremyresearch@iu.edu\n)\nStore, share, and collaborate on institutional files at IU\nAbout dedicated file storage services and IT services with storage components appropriate for sensitive institutional data, including research data containing protected health information\nApproved transcription services for all data domains\nThe following transcription services are appropriate for work with all institutional data domains:\nCarbonCopy\n:\nAvailable to IU students, faculty, and staff; for use with\nMicrosoft OneDrive at IU\nHuman-based transcription:\nNo\nAutomated transcription:\nYes\nApproved for FERPA:\nYes\nApproved for PHI:\nNo\nApproved for Critical research data (including human participant PII):\nApproval from the Data Steward for Research Data required; request approval by contacting\ndatard@iu.edu\nConditions for use:\nNo\nCost:\nNo fee (baseline service)\nContact:\nResearch Cloud Services (\nrcsadm@iu.edu\n)\nMicrosoft 365 Copilot app\n:\nFor use with secure Teams\nHuman-based transcription:\nNo\nAutomated transcription:\nYes\nHuman-based translation:\nNo\nAutomated translation:\nNo\nApproved for FERPA:\nYes\nApproved for PHI:\nYes\n1\nApproved for Critical research data (including human participant PII):\nNo\nConditions for use:\nYes\n2\nCost:\n$30/month per user license\nContact:\newahelp@iu.edu\nNotes:\nThis system or service meets certain requirements established in the\nHIPAA Security Rule\nthereby enabling its use for work involving data that contain protected health information (\nPHI\n). However, using this system or service does not fulfill your legal responsibilities for protecting the privacy and security of data that contain PHI. You may use this system or service for work involving data that contain PHI only if you institute additional\nadministrative\n,\nphysical\n, and\ntechnical\nsafeguards that complement those UITS already has in place.\nIf you have questions about managing HIPAA-regulated data at IU, email\nsecuremyresearch@iu.edu\n.\nThe Microsoft 365 Copilot app must be used with a secure Microsoft Teams space that is registered as containing Critical data. For more, see:\nUse Microsoft Teams to host meetings that contain protected health information (PHI)\nRequest institutional storage in Microsoft shared storage\nBest practices for Microsoft Teams at IU\nApproved transcription services for research and health data\nThe following transcription services are appropriate for work with research and health data; they have been reviewed and approved through the university's Third-Party Assessment (3PA) process, as required by university policy\nDisclosing Institutional Information to Third Parties (DM-02)\n:\nAbsolute Marketing and Research, LLC\n:\nMarketing research and support services company specializing in research transcripts and oral histories\nHuman-based transcription:\nYes\nAutomated transcription:\nNo\nHuman-based translation:\nNo\nAutomated translation:\nNo\nApproved for PHI:\nYes\n1\nApproved for Critical research data (including human participant PII):\nYes\nConditions for use:\nNo\nCost:\n30-day invoicing; transcripts invoiced based on character count plus spaces\nContact:\nSandy Keller (\nskeller@absoluteresearch.net\n)\nNote:\nA Business Associate Agreement (BAA) is in place.\nThis system or service meets certain requirements established in the\nHIPAA Security Rule\nthereby enabling its use for work involving data that contain protected health information (\nPHI\n). However, using this system or service does not fulfill your legal responsibilities for protecting the privacy and security of data that contain PHI. You may use this system or service for work involving data that contain PHI only if you institute additional\nadministrative\n,\nphysical\n, and\ntechnical\nsafeguards that complement those UITS already has in place.\nIf you have questions about managing HIPAA-regulated data at IU, email\nsecuremyresearch@iu.edu\n.\nAutomatic Sync Technologies\n:\nHuman-based transcription:\nNo\nAutomated transcription:\nYes\nHuman-based translation:\nYes\nAutomated translation:\nNo\nApproved for PHI:\nYes\n1\nApproved for Critical research data (including human participant PII):\nYes\nConditions for use:\nNo\nCost:\n$1.45/minute\nContact:\nLeslie Sands (\nleslie.s@mail.automaticsync.com\n)\nNote:\nA Business Associate Agreement (BAA) is in place.\nThis system or service meets certain requirements established in the\nHIPAA Security Rule\nthereby enabling its use for work involving data that contain protected health information (\nPHI\n). However, using this system or service does not fulfill your legal responsibilities for protecting the privacy and security of data that contain PHI. You may use this system or service for work involving data that contain PHI only if you institute additional\nadministrative\n,\nphysical\n, and\ntechnical\nsafeguards that complement those UITS already has in place.\nIf you have questions about managing HIPAA-regulated data at IU, email\nsecuremyresearch@iu.edu\n.\nAutomatic Transcription Service (ATS)\n:\nCollaboration between the Social Science Research Commons (\nSSRC\n), UITS Research Technologies, and the\nSecureMyResearch\nteam\nHuman-based transcription:\nNo\nAutomated transcription:\nYes\nHuman-based translation:\nNo\nAutomated translation:\nNo\nApproved for PHI:\nYes\n1\nApproved for Critical research data (including human participant PII): Yes\nConditions for use:\nYes\n2\nCost:\nAvailable to IU researchers at no cost\nContact:\nEmily Meanwell (\nemeanwel@iu.edu\n)\nNotes:\nA Business Associate Agreement (BAA) is in place.\nThis system or service meets certain requirements established in the\nHIPAA Security Rule\nthereby enabling its use for work involving data that contain protected health information (\nPHI\n). However, using this system or service does not fulfill your legal responsibilities for protecting the privacy and security of data that contain PHI. You may use this system or service for work involving data that contain PHI only if you institute additional\nadministrative\n,\nphysical\n, and\ntechnical\nsafeguards that complement those UITS already has in place.\nIf you have questions about managing HIPAA-regulated data at IU, email\nsecuremyresearch@iu.edu\n.\nSee "Requirements and Instructions" on the\nATS website\n. Researchers must first submit a\nnew project request form\n; once approved, ATS will send instructions for securely sending audio files to the ATS manager.\nGLOBO\n:\nHuman-based transcription:\nYes\nAutomated transcription:\nNo\nHuman-based translation:\nYes\nAutomated translation:\nNo\nApproved for PHI:\nYes\n1\nApproved for Critical research data (including human participant PII):\nYes\nConditions for use:\nNo\nCost:\n$30/minute\nContact:\nRebeca Buchan (\nasl@luna360.com\n)\nNote:\nA Business Associate Agreement (BAA) is in place.\nThis system or service meets certain requirements established in the\nHIPAA Security Rule\nthereby enabling its use for work involving data that contain protected health information (\nPHI\n). However, using this system or service does not fulfill your legal responsibilities for protecting the privacy and security of data that contain PHI. You may use this system or service for work involving data that contain PHI only if you institute additional\nadministrative\n,\nphysical\n, and\ntechnical\nsafeguards that complement those UITS already has in place.\nIf you have questions about managing HIPAA-regulated data at IU, email\nsecuremyresearch@iu.edu\n.\nInfraware\n:\nMedical transcription, education dictation and transcription services\nHuman-based transcription:\nYes\nAutomated transcription:\nNo\nHuman-based translation:\nNo\nAutomated translation:\nNo\nApproved for PHI:\nYes\n1\nApproved for Critical research data (including human participant PII):\nYes\nConditions for use:\n?\nCost:\n$4/minute\nContact:\nLaura Politte (\nLaura.Politte@InfraWare.com\n)\nNote:\nA Business Associate Agreement (BAA) is in place.\nThis system or service meets certain requirements established in the\nHIPAA Security Rule\nthereby enabling its use for work involving data that contain protected health information (\nPHI\n). However, using this system or service does not fulfill your legal responsibilities for protecting the privacy and security of data that contain PHI. You may use this system or service for work involving data that contain PHI only if you institute additional\nadministrative\n,\nphysical\n, and\ntechnical\nsafeguards that complement those UITS already has in place.\nIf you have questions about managing HIPAA-regulated data at IU, email\nsecuremyresearch@iu.edu\n.\nLandmark Associates, Inc.\n:\nTranscription and translation services to support research studies\nHuman-based transcription:\nYes\nAutomated transcription:\nNo\nHuman-based translation:\nYes\nAutomated translation:\nNo\nApproved for PHI:\nYes\n1\nApproved for Critical research data (including human participant PII):\nYes\nConditions for use:\nYes\nCost:\n$1.89/minute (standard rate)\n$1.69/minute (special faculty rate)\nContact:\nSofia Medina (\nsofiamedina@thelai.com\n)\nNote:\nA Business Associate Agreement (BAA) is in place.\nThis system or service meets certain requirements established in the\nHIPAA Security Rule\nthereby enabling its use for work involving data that contain protected health information (\nPHI\n). However, using this system or service does not fulfill your legal responsibilities for protecting the privacy and security of data that contain PHI. You may use this system or service for work involving data that contain PHI only if you institute additional\nadministrative\n,\nphysical\n, and\ntechnical\nsafeguards that complement those UITS already has in place.\nIf you have questions about managing HIPAA-regulated data at IU, email\nsecuremyresearch@iu.edu\n.\nLumivero\n(formerly QSR/NVivo):\nAutomated transcription service for audio and video recordings\nHuman-based transcription:\nNo\nAutomated transcription:\nYes\nHuman-based translation:\nNo\nAutomated translation:\nNo\nApproved for PHI:\nNo\nApproved for Critical research data (including human participant PII):\nYes\nConditions for use:\nYes\n1\nCost:\nNo cost\nContact:\nDave Kolodny (\ndkolodny@lumivero.com\n)\nNote:\nUsers must delete files from the Lumivero platform within 30 days of uploading and maintain copies on appropriate IU managed systems, such as\nMicrosoft at IU Secure Storage\n.\nMicrosoft 365 transcription:\nSeveral options for creating transcripts are available as part of\nMicrosoft 365 at IU\n. Word allows you to dictate directly into a document and to upload an audio file for transcription; for instructions, see\nTranscribe your recordings\n. SharePoint allows you to create captions or transcriptions associated with audio and video files; for instructions, see\nAdd captions or transcripts to audio and video assets in a SharePoint space\nand\nView, edit, and manage video transcripts and captions\n.\nHuman-based transcription:\nNo\nAutomated transcription:\nYes\nHuman-based translation:\nNo\nAutomated translation:\nNo\nApproved for PHI:\nYes\n1\nApproved for Critical research data (including human participant PII):\nYes\nConditions for use:\nYes\n2\nCost:\nNo cost\nContact:\newahelp@iu.edu\nNote:\nThis system or service meets certain requirements established in the\nHIPAA Security Rule\nthereby enabling its use for work involving data that contain protected health information (\nPHI\n). However, using this system or service does not fulfill your legal responsibilities for protecting the privacy and security of data that contain PHI. You may use this system or service for work involving data that contain PHI only if you institute additional\nadministrative\n,\nphysical\n, and\ntechnical\nsafeguards that complement those UITS already has in place.\nIf you have questions about managing HIPAA-regulated data at IU, email\nsecuremyresearch@iu.edu\n.\nThe Microsoft 365 Copilot app must be used with a secure Microsoft Teams space that is registered as containing\nCritical data\n. For more, see:\nUse Microsoft Teams to host meetings that contain protected health information (PHI)\nRequest institutional storage in Microsoft shared storage\nBest practices for Microsoft Teams at IU\nSonix.ai\n:\nHuman-based transcription:\nNo\nAutomated transcription:\nYes\nHuman-based translation:\nNo\nAutomated translation:\nYes\nApproved for PHI:\nNo\nApproved for Critical research data (including human participant PII):\nYes\nConditions for use:\nNo\nCost:\nSee\nhttps://sonix.ai/pricing\nContact:\nwecare@sonix.ai\nAccessibility service that may also provide transcription\nThe following accessibility services may provide transcription services; check\nBUY.IU\nfor current contact information:\nAI-Media\n(formerly Alternative Communications Services, LLC)\nSeeWriteHear, LLC\nTranscription services not approved for use with institutional data\nThe following transcription services are not approved for use with institutional data at IU:\nTemi\nor\nRev\nGMR Transcription\nOtter.ai	KB0026447	KB0026447 v24.0	 domains: CarbonCopy: Available to IU students, faculty, and staff; for use with Microsoft <strong>OneDrive</strong> at IU	1.8867		2026-01-31 16:55:10.171256	2026-01-31 16:55:10.171256	0	9ccedd7e47743ad42fc6a55b416d43fc
10853	https://servicenow.iu.edu/kb?id=kb_article_view&sys_kb_id=e90e64a24726be18d500b87b716d4348	External tools available in Canvas	Table of contents\nOverview\nTools under review\nAssessment\nCommunication (real-time and asynchronous)\nContent creation, presentation, and management\nCourse management\nDigital courseware and learning tools\nLibrary research\nMiscellaneous\nSIS integration\nStudent success\nOverview\nBelow is a list of external tools (also called LTI tools, LTI apps, or external apps) that have been reviewed and approved for use at Indiana University. Most are available in all Canvas courses, but some are restricted by campus, school, or department to comply with licensing agreements or other constraints.\nMost of the tools integrated with Canvas are available for use by students, faculty, and staff without fee because IU or a sponsoring unit is covering the licensing costs. Exceptions (noted below) include online textbooks and digital courseware and learning tools offered by textbook publishers.\nA few of the tools on this page are either included in your course navigation menu, or appear in other parts of the Canvas user interface. Most, however, are hidden, which means you'll need to expose them if you want to use them. For more about installing and exposing external tools, see\nAdd an external app to your course in Canvas\n.\nImportant:\nAs an instructor, if you use an application managed by a supplier with whom IU does not have a contract, and it collects protected student data, you may be subject to sanctions, according to university policy\nDisclosing Institutional Information to Third Parties (DM-02)\n. If your intended use will collect any\nFERPA\n-protected data in a third-party tool,\ndo not\nuse it before working through appropriate institutional offices to get a contract with the service. For guidance, see\nCloud resources for teaching\nand/or consult your campus\nteaching and learning center\n.\nTools under review\nThe following tools are currently being evaluated and are available on a limited basis through the Next.IU pilot program or campus-specific pilots. To learn more about the Next.IU initiative or sign up for a pilot, go to\nNext.IU\n.\nDelphinium\n:\nGamify your gradebook to increase student motivation in courses, personalize communication with students based on data, and visualize progress with customizable dashboards and a leaderboard.\nMy Learning Analytics (MyLA)\n:\nMonitor your academic progress and compare it to others in your class.\nTerracotta\n:\nEmbed studies in course sites to conduct experimental research on teaching and learning.\nAssessment\nCourse Questionnaire (OCQ)\nCourse Questionnaire (OCQ)\n:\nConduct mid-term and end-of-semester course evaluations/questionnaires\nQuestionnaire Responses\n:\nView Course Questionnaire results\nBoth tools available to all courses, except:\nNot available at the School of Medicine\nIn Fort Wayne, OCQ and Questionnaire Responses are limited to courses in the Schools of Health Sciences, Nursing, and Social Work.\nExamSoft\n:\nCreate and analyze computer-based exams, and prevent students from accessing local and online resources while taking exams\nAvailable only at the IU School of Medicine\nGradescope\n:\nGrade bubble sheets, hand-written assignments and problems, and coding assignments\nAvailable to all courses\nHonorlock\n:\nThird-party proctoring of online tests\nAvailable under certain conditions; for current policy and procedure, see\nAbout online proctoring at IU\n.\nKaltura Quizzing\n:\nAdd auto-graded questions to a video stored in Kaltura\nAvailable to all courses\nLockDown Browser\n:\nPrevent students from accessing external resources while taking quizzes in Canvas\nAvailable to all courses\nQM Advantage\n:\nConduct an informal review of your online course using the Quality Matters standards\nAvailable to all courses\nQuick Check\nAvailable to all courses\nRegisterBlast\n:\nSchedule proctored exam times at the IU Indianapolis Testing Center\nAvailable only on the Indianapolis campus\nTaskstream Learning Achievement Tools\nTaskstream:\nAssess student performance based on established outcomes and standards\nTaskstream Assignments:\nCreate, submit, or grade a Taskstream assignment in Canvas\nBoth Taskstream tools are limited to Schools of Education at the Indianapolis and South Bend campuses\nThe Taskstream service is no longer widely used at IU, and is no longer supported by UITS. Support is now provided directly by the departments using the service. Additionally, you can email Watermark Support at\nsupport@watermarkinsights.com\n.\nTop Hat\n:\nAsk questions and collect student responses in class\nAvailable to all courses\nTrueLearn\n:\nAvailable only in the IUSM node (and all subaccounts under IUSM)\nTurnitin\nTurnitin Plagiarism Framework\n:\nUse Turnitin for plagiarism detection\nTurnitin LTI tool\n:\nUse grading and feedback tools available in Turnitin Feedback Studio (PeerMark, QuickMarks, Turnitin Rubrics, and automated spelling and grammar checking)\nBoth Turnitin tools are available to all courses\nView'em\n:\nPost a spreadsheet with scores, feedback, or other types of data for students to view\nAvailable to all courses\nAssessment digital learning tools\nGoReact\n:\nAssess or collaborate with students on performance-based skills\nMust be ordered through IU eTexts; involves a student fee\nAvailable to all courses\nMust be added to your course by a Canvas administrator\nCommunication (real-time and asynchronous)\nCanvas Notifier\n:\nSend a Canvas message to a specific list of users\nAvailable to all courses\nInScribe 2.0\n:\nCreate a learning support system that connects educators and learners\nAvailable to all courses\nMicrosoft Education\n:\nCreate a team in\nMicrosoft Teams\nand synchronize it with your Canvas course roster\nAvailable to all courses\nMulticourse Announcements\n:\nPost an announcement to multiple courses at the same time\nAvailable to all courses\nMulticourse Messages\n:\nSend a Canvas message to two or more courses at the same time\nAvailable to all courses\nZoom\n:\nParticipate in real-time web conferencing sessions\nAvailable to all courses\nCommunication digital learning tools\nPiazza\n:\nAsk and answer questions in an asynchronous discussion format\nMust be ordered through IU eTexts; involves a student fee\nMust be added to your course by a Canvas administrator\nVoiceThread\n:\nAsynchronous discussions with a focus on visual media, such as documents, photographs, slides, and videos\nMust be ordered through IU eTexts; involves a student fee\nMust be added to your course by a Canvas administrator\nContent creation, presentation, and management\nNote:\nYou can also find some tools that allow you to present content to students in the\nDigital courseware and learning tools\nand\nLibrary research\nsections below.\nAcademic Video Online\n:\nAccess over 70,000 videos in subject areas including anthropology, business, counseling, film, health, history, and music\nAvailable only at IU Indianapolis\nAdobe Creative Cloud\n:\nAccess Adobe Creative Cloud tools to create presentations, graphics, and videos\nAvailable to all courses\nAlly\n:\nLearn how to make your course more accessible\nAutomatically added to all courses, with no way for it to be removed\nBroadcast\n:\nDistribute files to student accounts in\nMicrosoft OneDrive at IU\nAvailable to all courses\nCanvas Commons\n:\nStore, find, import, and share course materials via the Canvas learning object repository\nAvailable to all courses\nCidi Labs DesignPLUS suite\nDesignPLUS Sidebar\n:\nAdvanced editor for any Canvas tool that uses the rich content editor, except New Quizzes. Primarily for instructional designers.\nMulti-Tool\n:\nEasily create/edit course templates and module structure and manage availability dates for all dated items\nTidyUp\n:\nFind, download, and remove unused files, folders, and Canvas content (pages, assignments, quizzes, and discussion topics) in your course\nUpload/Embed Image\n:\nFind, upload, download, size, crop, and rotate images in the Canvas rich content editor\nAll tools available to all courses\nGoogle at IU\nGoogle Assignments\n:\nCreate\nGoogle at IU\nMy Drive\nassignments and embed\nGoogle My Drive\ncontent\nGoogle Course Tools\n:\nCreate\nGoogle Drive\nfolders and\nGoogle Groups\nfor your course\nGoogle Drive\n:\nAccess, share, and collaborate on content stored in\nGoogle at IU\naccounts\nAll Google tools available to all courses\nIU Media Collections Online\n:\nAccess audio and video recordings from IU collections and select scholarly projects\nAvailable to all courses except at the IU School of Medicine\nKaltura\nKaltura: Media Gallery\n:\nCreate and manage a media collection for your course\nKaltura: My Media\n:\nCreate and manage media in your personal collection in Kaltura\nBoth tools available to all courses\nLinkedIn Learning\n:\nMake LinkedIn Learning courses available to students as graded assignments or as part of a module\nAvailable to all courses\nMediaSite\n:\nCreate and manage media in MediaSite, a video capture and management platform\nAvailable only to courses in the IU School of Medicine and the IN-DAST, IN-DENT, and IN-DHYG departments at IU Indianapolis\nPlayPosit\n:\nIncorporate questions, reflections, web overlays, and other types of interactions into course videos\nNote:\nOn December 29, 2025, PlayPosit will change its name to WeVideo.  For details, see\nAbout the change from PlayPosit to WeVideo\n.\nAvailable to all courses\nPressbooks\n:\nCreate an eBook and share it with your class\nAvailable to all courses\nMust be added to your course by a Canvas administrator\nYouTube\n:\nSearch for, embed, and view publicly accessible YouTube videos\nAvailable to all courses\nContent creation, presentation, and management digital learning tools\nHypothesis\n:\nCollaboratively annotate PDFs and web resources or assign annotation tasks to students\nMust be ordered through IU eTexts; involves a s