11238	https://servicenow.iu.edu/kb?id=kb_article_view&sys_kb_id=caffa4bb476456583d373803846d435a	Scheduled maintenance for UITS systems	To keep Indiana University computing systems, services, and networks functioning optimally,\nUITS\nsystem administrators have implemented a schedule of regularly occurring maintenance windows. During its regularly scheduled maintenance window, a particular IU computing system, service, or network will most likely be unavailable to its users. Even if downtime is not required, you should use\nextreme caution\nwhen using a system or service during its scheduled maintenance window; any changes you make during a maintenance window may not be saved.\nTo view the list of regularly scheduled maintenance windows (that is, downtimes) for UITS computing systems, services, and networks, see Status.IU's\nRegularly scheduled maintenance windows\n.\nAdditionally, on the day they occur, system and service downtimes are posted on\nStatus.IU\n.\nUITS considers scheduled downtimes for performing routine maintenance a vital part of its normal procedures for delivering robust information technology services.\nFor help, contact your campus\nSupport Center\n.	KB0024385	KB0024385 v1.0	To keep Indiana University <strong>computing</strong> systems, services, and networks functioning optimally, UITS its regularly scheduled maintenance window, a particular IU <strong>computing</strong> system, service, or network windows (that is, downtimes) for UITS <strong>computing</strong> systems, services, and networks, see Status.IU's	106.2596		2026-01-31 17:03:09.099184	2026-01-31 17:04:19.274124	0	caffa4bb476456583d373803846d435a
11262	https://servicenow.iu.edu/kb?id=kb_article_view&sys_kb_id=44ffe87b476456583d373803846d43a2	Access VoiceOver at IU	Overview\nVoiceOver is the built-in screen reader that comes with MacOS and iOS. Listed below are the different ways you can access VoiceOver while at IU.\nAccess VoiceOver\nPersonal computer\nVoiceOver is built into your macOS computer to use. To learn more about VoiceOver, see the\nVoiceOver Getting Started Guide\n.\nSTC computing labs\nVoiceOver is available in the macOS-based STC computing labs across all of the IU campuses. To find STC computing labs for your IU campus, see\nAbout the IU STCs (computing labs)\n.\nFor instructions on accessing VoiceOver in the STCs, see\nAccess VoiceOver in the STC computing labs\n.\nLearn more\nVoiceOver basics\nVoiceOver for iOS basics\nVoiceOver commands and gestures on Mac\nUITS staff and local UITS support:\nWhen a\nclient\nrequires additional support with this application:\nTransfer emergency requests to the\nAssistive Technology and Accessibility Centers\n(\nATAC\n) at 812-856-4112.\nFor non-emergency requests (or if the\nclient\ncannot speak to the\nATAC\n), gather the following information, and then escalate the issue by assigning it to\nAssistive Technology and Accessibility Centers\nin ServiceNow:\nName\nIU username\nContact email address and/or phone number\nA description of the issue (make sure that you\ndo not\ninclude any of the\nclient\n's medical- or condition-related information in the ticket)\nThe\nATAC\n's hours of operation are Monday-Friday 8am-5pm. Assign any support issues received after hours to\nAssistive Technology and Accessibility Centers\nin ServiceNow.	KB0024219	KB0024219 v1.0	 Started Guide. STC <strong>computing</strong> labs VoiceOver is available in the macOS-based STC <strong>computing</strong> labs across all of the IU campuses. To find STC <strong>computing</strong> labs for your IU campus, see About the IU STCs (<strong>computing</strong> labs). For instructions on accessi