6224	https://servicenow.iu.edu/kb?id=kb_article_view&sys_kb_id=12afe837476456583d373803846d438f	Get additional IU computing accounts	Table of contents\nRequirements\nInstructions\nRequirements\nYou are eligible to create computing accounts and access information technology services at Indiana University; for eligibility requirements, see\nComputing accounts at IU\n.\nYou have already created your IU basic computing accounts; if you haven't, or you are a former student returning to IU after an absence (for example, a graduate student who was once an IU undergraduate), see\nCreate your first IU computing accounts (admitted students, faculty, staff, affiliates, and those returning to IU)\n.\nFor group accounts, see\nAbout group and departmental accounts\n. For student organization accounts, see\nComputing accounts for IU Bloomington and IU Indianapolis student organizations\n.\nInstructions\nGo to\nCreate More Accounts\n.\nGroup accounts:\nIn a fresh browser in which you have not logged into\nIU Login\n, navigate to\nManage Your Email\n. Log in using your group account credentials.\nSelect\nCreate Computing Account\n.\nYou will see listed the accounts you are eligible to create. Select the appropriate account, and follow the prompts.\nNote:\nWhen creating an account on an IU system administered by\nUITS\nResearch Technologies\n, you will be prompted for additional information; see\nQuestions you'll need to answer when requesting research computing accounts\n.\nNote:\nIf you are eligible for an account but you are not presented with\nthe option to create it, try the process again. If you still cannot create the account,\ncontact your\ncampus Support Center\n.	KB0022647	KB0022647 v1.0	Table of contents Requirements Instructions Requirements You are eligible to create <strong>computing</strong>, see <strong>Computing</strong> accounts at IU. You have already created your IU basic <strong>computing</strong> accounts who was once an IU undergraduate), see Create your first IU <strong>computing</strong> accounts (admitted students	131.7374		2026-01-31 14:51:36.987984	2026-01-31 17:02:57.213826	0	12afe837476456583d373803846d438f
6265	https://servicenow.iu.edu/kb?id=kb_article_view&sys_kb_id=34ffac7b476456583d373803846d439b	Overview of IU computing accounts when students, faculty, or staff leave IU	Your eligibility to access and use Indiana University information technology resources is dependent upon your\nstatus with IU\n. The scope of access and use varies according to your status; for example, some IU computing accounts are available only to IU employees, and some are available only to IU students.\nAccording to IU's\nEligibility to Use Information Technology Resources (IT-03)\npolicy, your eligibility to access and use IU computing accounts and resources, including\nlicensed software\n, ceases when you no longer have the IU status that supports that eligibility. For example, if you are an enrolled student and part-time hourly employee at IU, and then you end your IU employment while maintaining your enrollment as an IU student, you become ineligible to access and use certain computing resources that were available to you at work but retain your eligibility to access and use computing resources available to enrolled IU students.\nRole-specific information for when you leave IU:\nStudents:\nStudent computing accounts, data, and software when you leave IU\nNote:\nIf you are transferring from one IU campus to another, leaving IU temporarily to study abroad, or entering active military service, see\nStudent computing accounts when you transfer campuses, study abroad, or have active military service\n.\nFaculty, staff, hourly employees, and IU affiliates:\nEmployee computing accounts when you leave IU\nNote:\nOfficially retired faculty and staff members are eligible to access and use certain IU computing resources; for details, see\nAccess to IU resources for official IU retirees\n.	KB0024289	KB0024289 v1.0	, some IU <strong>computing</strong> accounts are available only to IU employees, and some are available only to IU eligibility to access and use IU <strong>computing</strong> accounts and