6272	https://servicenow.iu.edu/kb?id=kb_article_view&sys_kb_id=2e656005477e3694d500b87b716d434e	Contact your campus IT Support Center	Table of contents\nOverview\nIU Bloomington\nIU Indianapolis\nIU Columbus\nIU East\nIU Fort Wayne\nIU Kokomo\nIU Northwest\nIU South Bend\nIU Southeast\nOverview\nThe UITS Support Center provides IT support to all IU campuses. So that Support Center staff can efficiently assist you,\nbe ready to provide details about your problem or question\n.\nAlternatively, try using\nAskIT\nto answer your question by selecting the widget in the lower right corner.\nNotes:\nIn-person (formerly walk-in) support hours:\nThe hours listed below for in-person support locations are for periods when classes are in session. In-person support hours during campus breaks and between semesters may vary.\nResearch computing support:\nResearch computing support at IU is provided by the\nResearch Technologies\ndivision of\nUITS\n. To ask a question or get help regarding\nResearch Technologies\nservices, including IU's\nresearch supercomputers\nand research storage systems, and the scientific,  statistical, and mathematical applications available on those systems,\ncontact UITS\nResearch Technologies\n. For service-specific support contact information, see\nResearch computing support at IU\n.\nDuo tokens:\nDuo tokens are available\nonly\nat the Wells Library (Bloomington), Indianapolis, and Kokomo locations.\nBloomington\nContact\nWith the exception of special holiday hours, phone, email, and chat support is available 7am-11pm daily. During holiday closures, phone calls will route to the\nUITS Contact Center\nfor an answering service.\nChat:\nhttps://chataiu.ea.iu.edu/askit\nPhone: 812-855-6789\nEmail:\nithelp@iu.edu\nWeb form:\nSubmit an IT support request\nOnline:\nKnowledge Base\nIn-person support\nIn-person support at the Herman B Wells Library (LI 401 on the fourth floor of the West Tower) is available as follows:\nMonday-Thursday: 8am-8pm\nFriday: 8am-7:30pm